
# PyInstaller output. Regenerable from App.spec (`pyinstaller App.spec`), and
# App.pkg alone was 93 MB -- over the 50 MB house limit and close enough to
# GitHub's 100 MB hard ceiling to break a push one day.
HOF Scripts/Python Visualizer/**/build/
HOF Scripts/Python Visualizer/**/dist/
*.pkg
*.pyz

# BARRY's error log travels by Supabase now, not by git.
#
# It was append-only JSONL per machine per day, committed to the repo, and
# that commit was the only way one machine's errors reached another -- so a
# colleague's crash was invisible until somebody remembered to commit and
# somebody else remembered to pull. It also accumulated in the history of a
# repo that is meant to hold recordings and decisions.
#
# The files stay on disk as the offline buffer: BARRY records an error
# whether or not there is a network, which is exactly when it matters most.
# They are cache now, not transport.
_Jarvis/app/GUI_logs/errors/

# The activity log, for the same reason and with the same trade.
#
# Ninety-five kinds of action, several thousand lines a week, one file per
# machine per day -- and committing them was the only way one person's
# history reached another. So the repository carried a growing pile of
# keystroke records, and "who loaded this recording last" was still
# unanswerable until somebody remembered to push.
#
# It goes through Supabase now, and the History view can query the whole
# lab's. The files stay on disk as the offline buffer: BARRY records what
# happened whether or not there is a network, which is exactly when it
# matters. They are cache, not transport.
_Jarvis/app/GUI_logs/activity/

# How long each stage of a comodulogram took on THIS machine, so the progress
# bar's estimate is right on the rig as well as on a laptop. Per machine by
# nature and worthless anywhere else -- committing it would mean two computers
# overwriting each other's timings to no purpose.
_Jarvis/app/GUI_logs/.cfc_rates.json

# The launchers folder (2026-11-03). Its shortcut is made on each Windows
# machine by backend/launchers.py and holds that machine's absolute paths,
# so it can never be shared; Finder's .DS_Store files are nobody's work.
_Jarvis/Activate Jarvis.lnk
.DS_Store

# The app folder before 2026-11-03. git moved everything it tracked into
# _Jarvis/app; what a pull leaves behind here is machine-local by
# definition (the Supabase key, the VACC sign-in, the review key, caches)
# and must never be committed. Jarvis carries it across on its first start
# (backend/launchers.py leftovers).
/BARRY GUI/

# Plain-text sign-ins: never committed (the repo is public). See backend/softmouse_login.py.
user_pass.txt
